=== task: cells easy
title: Which bucket?
prompt: A hash map with 6 buckets puts each integer key into bucket `key % 6`. Which bucket does each key go into?
labels: 13 | 24 | 6 | 40
answer: 1 | 0 | 0 | 4
wrong[1 | 4 | 6 | 4]: 24 % 6 is 0, because 24 is 4 × 6 exactly; and there's no bucket 6: 6 % 6 is 0.
wrong[2 | 4 | 1 | 6]: That divides instead of taking the remainder.
hint: The remainder after dividing by 6 is between 0 and 5.
